WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.620
 I think the first is depending on how well you want to do, particularly if you're starting

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.020
 a company, you need to work super hard.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:17.300
 So what does super hard mean?

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:22.220
 Well, when my brother and I were starting our first company, instead of getting an apartment,

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:27.060
 we just rented a small office and we slept on the couch.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:35.420
 We shared at the YMCA and we had just one computer, so the website was up during the day and

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:51.760
 I was coding at night, seven days a week all the time.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:57.480
 Every card, every waking hour, that's the thing I would say, particularly if you're starting

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:58.480
 a company.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.260
 And if you do a simple math to say, "Okay, if somebody else is working 50 hours and you're

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:07.440
 working 100," you'll get twice as much done in the course of a year as the other company.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:32.680
 I think, too, is you've got to make sure that whatever you're doing is a great product

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:33.680
 or service.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:34.680
 It has to be really great.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:40.060
 And I go back to what I was saying earlier, where if you're a new company, unless it's

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:46.880
 like some new industry or new market, if it's an untapped market, then you have more ability

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:51.120
 to, the standard is lower for your product or service, but if you're entering anything

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:57.960
 where there's an existing marketplace against large entrenched competitors, then your product

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.160
 or service needs to be much better than theirs.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.480
 It can't be a little bit better because then you put yourself in the shoes of the consumer

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.280
 and they say, "Why would you buy it as a consumer?

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:10.280
 You're always going to buy the trusted brand unless there's a big difference."

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:16.920
 So a lot of times, one entrepreneur will come up with something which is only slightly better.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.400
 It can't just be slightly better.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:30.440
 It's got to be a lot better.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:37.600
 The other thing I'd say is that if you're creating a company or if you're joining a company,

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:41.040
 the most important thing is to attract great people.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:45.720
 So either join a group that's amazing that you really respect or if you're building

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.160
 a company, you've got to gather great people.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:50.840
 I mean, all the company is, is a group of people that have gathered together to create

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.560
 a product or service.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:56.760
 And so depending upon how talented and hardworking that group is and the degree to which they

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:02.480
 are focused cohesively in a good direction, that will determine the success of the company.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:14.500
 So do everything you can to gather great people if you're creating a company.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:21.760
 Then, I'd say focus on signal over noise.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.120
 A lot of companies get confused.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:28.640
 They spend money on things that don't actually make the product better.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:33.520
 So for example, at Tesla, we've never spent any money on advertising.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:39.240
 We've put all of the money into R&D and manufacturing and design to try to make the car as good

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.840
 as possible.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:44.240
 And I think that's the way to go.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:49.040
 So if we're in a given company, just keep thinking about are these efforts that people

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.040
 are expanding?

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.840
 Are they resulting in a better product or service?

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.640
 And if they're not, stop those efforts.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:08.920
 And then I think the final thing I would encourage you to do is, now is the time to

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:10.680
 take risk.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:17.840
 You don't have kids, but as you get older, your obligations increase.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:21.960
 And once you have a family, you start taking risk not just for yourself, but for your family

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:22.960
 as well.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:26.720
 It gets much harder to do things that might not work out.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:31.560
 So now is the time to do that before you have those obligations.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:35.760
 So I would encourage you to take risks and not do something bold.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:36.280
 You won't regret it.

